strengths.value:
### Strong points:

1) Utilizing $\alpha$-policy to deal with the influence of analytical policy gradients when training;

2) Adopting criteria to detect/calculate variance and bias;

3) An algorithm was designed to handle the strength of analytical gradients during updating;

4) Empirical results look good.

By the way, in the Supplementary Materials, the author(s) provided a mp4 video file, where the animation on the scenario of the traffic problem looks fantastic. Thanks for providing that.

